WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.238
Step five removes the
security profile's links.

2
00:00:03.238 --> 00:00:06.738
The T L S inspection policy
comes out in Learn's order:

3
00:00:06.738 --> 00:00:12.112
unlink it from the pilot profile, delete
the policy, then remove the certificate.

4
00:00:12.112 --> 00:00:14.988
The filtering policy's Conditional Access

5
00:00:14.988 --> 00:00:17.863
policy goes to disabled,
the Step 5 rollback.

6
00:00:17.863 --> 00:00:21.042
Step six turns off tenant
restrictions tagging;

7
00:00:21.042 --> 00:00:24.063
the tenant restrictions
policy itself stays.

8
00:00:24.063 --> 00:00:27.900
Step seven takes the groups out
of each profile's assignments

9
00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:31.212
in the admin center, then
disables the three profiles.

10
00:00:31.212 --> 00:00:35.862
In production, the next line of the
rollback is restoring the V P N route.

11
00:00:35.862 --> 00:00:41.174
Step eight turns off signaling, last,
now that no policy enforces on it.

12
00:00:41.174 --> 00:00:43.321
Step nine takes the export again,

13
00:00:43.321 --> 00:00:48.330
so the evidence shows the state after
the rollback: three profiles disabled,

14
00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:52.225
signaling and tagging disabled,
and no test policy enabled.

15
00:00:52.225 --> 00:00:57.214
Steps ten to twelve clean up: delete
the test policies, apps, profile and

16
00:00:57.214 --> 00:01:02.375
filtering policy; remove the QUIC
rule; and delete the telemetry setting.

17
00:01:02.375 --> 00:01:08.000
In production, that last one ends the
evidence trail and happens only by change.

18
00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.620
Keep the lab folder; it's
the path's evidence package.
